{"text": "May 15,2014\n\nIn the interest of better managing the demand for and production of public records I'd\nlike to make the following suggestions:\n\n+ Once CAFI\u2019s Public Records Portal is operational, all public records requests\n(PRRs) should be made through and/or tracked by the on-line system. Chris\nPersuad is developing the Portal for the Foundation at a cost of about $1,500. The\nPortal is expected to be fully operational within the next two to three weeks. The\nPortal will allow secure access from any Internet connection and tracks the\nfollowing categories of data:\n\u00a9 Sending and receiving PRRs via email\n\u00a9 Agencies (both publicly operated agencies and vendors)\n\u00a9 People (contacts with various agencies and vendors)\n\u00a9 Contracts (both state and local vendors, including the actual contract,\ndocuments)\nAILPRRs regardless of form (email, USPS, in-person, telephonic, ete.)\nAll interactions with agencies relating to a PRR\n\u00a9 Projects Management (these include on-going multilayered projects like\nthe School Resource Officers, School Bus Safety, Specialty License\nPlates, etc.)\n\noo\n\nIn addition to the ability to track and manage PRRs the Portal will allow us to\n\u2018generate customized reports. For example, we can run reports that show any\nunanswered PRRs, any PRRs that are more than 30 days old, how many PRRs\nhave been made within the past week, how many denials we've had, and how\n\u2018many matters have been referred to attomneys for litigation. The list of reports is\nalmost limitless.\n\n\u2018+ Until the Portal is operational (again, I expect this it to be on-line within two to\nthree weeks) I'd like all PRRs to be sent to me for review before they go out.\nThis is something I\u2019m already doing with Cathy Zollo and Dylan Bouscher\n(\u201cDylan the Inter\u201d). My rational is that since I make so many PRRs I'd like to\nhave some idea about what is being done so we don\u2019t duplicate efforts and in the\nevent that litigation unfortunately becomes necessary, I'd like to be sure we have\nthe best possible set of facts.\n\u2018+ Until the Portal is operational I'd also like any written PRRs (email, USPS, etc.)\nto be made using the template that I provided a couple of weeks ago. This is\nsomething that has been developed and refined over the years and has been vetted\nby numerous public records litigators, the First Amendment Foundation, ete.\n\n1280 West Newport Center Drive Deerfield Beach, Florida 33442\n(88) 830-3769 / Info@CitizensAwarenessFoundation org\nwww.CitizensAwarenessFoundation.org",
